notes:
Greptile (PR #28) flagged two issues in the scaffolding code added in this feature branch:

1. state.rs:304 - _wiki_links_need_update is computed but immediately discarded (dead computation). The _ prefix suppresses the warning but doesn't clarify intent. Greptile recommends a // TODO(marky-77x) comment instead.

2. state.rs:289 - Incomplete overlap check: the single-line column check fires only when edit_start_line == edit_end_line == range.start.line. Multi-line edits that END on a link's start line skip the column check, producing false positives (unnecessary rebuilds). The check is currently unused so no runtime impact, but the bug should be fixed before wiring in marky-77x.

Suggested fix for #2:
  // edit ends on the link's start line — check column overlap on the end side
  if edit_end_line == range.start.line {
      let link_start = range.start.character;
      return edit_end_col > link_start;
  }
